-95693" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{2{e}^{2x}}{\\sqrt{{e}^{4x}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "This integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${e}^{4x}={({e}^{2x})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u={e}^{2x}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2{e}^{2x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2{e}^{2x}}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and compute it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2{e}^{2x}}{\\sqrt{{e}^{4x}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{2{e}^{2x}}{\\sqrt{{({e}^{2x})}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{2u}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2u}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{e}^{2x}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-95693/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20b69474-34f6-5539-accf-5ebfc4f6eb0a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95693"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-95692/selection/3e5e0084143f4cb504f2648d29f93b301a0f3138709468136d8e5fc88e1c1f56" :answer/id #uuid "7c998079-0ccf-5d38-ad43-c6503efa6137" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\,x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95692/selection/dfdaa7de7eacb39ab18979c5e28e4e1cb18b3d5aa7fd158624b300977d3bb8c4" :answer/id #uuid "7f1e9266-5072-59d6-814f-3e713f2e875a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\,x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95692/selection/fe37d0a0f618aafa97a0e44903dd97cd287c120c989329d03ca3ced51ce1355c" :answer/id #uuid 