stion/id #uuid "b73c27f0-6c57-5652-a89b-fec017279303" :question/math-academy-id "q-95853" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-25}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-25}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{5}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{x}{5})}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic cosine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{5})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{5}.$ Differentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{5}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=5\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-25}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{5}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{x}{5})}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot 5\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\frac{x}{5})+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-95853/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "25d92a33-95e8-5860-b461-8291dac502d6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95853"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-95850/selection/4e59e9c772f38d6946e420bf7c6d2092623509392eefa7e5fb52ffb34e51106b" :answer/id #uuid "f7fdacdd-4727-5f84-9371-08e495ea53e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡3x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95850/selection/878a7316f265c7d1c7940d76e7e8315ea75df7eb6393d8d6ceee0cc875958f24" :answer/id #uuid "12e6fe83-8aa2-53c0-8e3b-5c4579e6198c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡3x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95850/selection/3791d9fab21664ed4d234f5d214d12becd7801d441d16725c255edaf98f5fff6" :answer/id #uuid "0c34f64d-bd8d-50fc-8567-bc541f1a4649" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡3x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95850/selection/96d3cc3e23b1e21366a7afe81dafd35b422ddb7bda8389611b31087162d69bc6" :answer/id #uuid "dc4ea9da-f95a-53c9-be74-f645572840a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡3x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95850/selection/147052b6b905a08676f818a3187526d308d9d4a1fe06b130794f7f85b71ddd3a" :answer/id #uuid "747b8a74-f7e2-5907-a0f5-5ade5c1f1c09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡3x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95850/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b9b28e2c-70ab-53a7-a766-c887a7508eb0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-95850/selection/4e59e9c772f38d6946e420bf7c6d2092623509392eefa7e5fb52ffb34e51106b" :answer-field/choices ["q-95850/selection/4e59e9c772f38d6946e420bf7c6d2092623509392eefa7e5fb52ffb34e51106b" "q-95850/selection/878a7316f265c7d1c7940d76e7e8315ea75df7eb6393d8d6ceee0cc875958f24" "q-95850/selection/3791d9fab21664ed4d234f5d214d12becd7801d441d16725c255edaf98f5fff6" "q-95850/selection/96d3cc3e23b1e21366a7afe81dafd35b422ddb7bda8389611b31087162d69bc6" "q-95850/selection/147052b6b905a08676f818a3187526d308d9d4a1fe06b130794f7f85b71ddd3a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-95850" :question/id #uuid "c2b64b0d-0000-5979-8de5-6e569bc1ff99" :question/math-academy-id "q-95850" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "This integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic cosine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $9{x}^{2}=(3x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=3x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and compute it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(3x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡3x+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-95850/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "25d92a33-95e8-5860-b461-8291dac502d6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95850"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-95855/selection/275f2b7895b40a849c888b5402ddbc680e1eb74fc3147bd6bdd76c9795e8136e" :answer/id #uuid "3410c07a-9fd5-5a34-a131-2ef10206d2fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "49\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{x}{7})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95855/selection/5a8ec005d5367a55746e4c735aea4a018c54dcd5f558b6e8f30413b74904d0e6" :answer/id #uuid "541959be-7673-51f9-8af9-b828a3d2235d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{x}{7})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95855/selection/a62f421674b77003c20b046ca2f8b65897070ff90afd4d6e9e955e55f1d0f3be" :answer/id #uuid "502cb510-2f8e-50c5-adbe-8fa621516a2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\frac{x}{7})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95855/selection/8a8e1971997c1605d4368db29647043a3de54ca1318b4871c8b4de72b1e51533" :answer/id #uuid "254ff030-a1c6-5e81-bb54-cfc1d937efd3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\operat